  "scientific_review": [
    "All20declared latitude sections were acquired at exactJanuary15/July15,2022T00Z. Retain every native longitude column,raw east/north velocities,signed geographic components,all candidate scores,qualifying local maxima,source indices,actual timestamps and source attributes. Full40-level native depth profiles extend0–5000m;missing/dry cells remain null.",
    "All gates are exploratory OSW choices declared before viewing new field outcomes,not source numerical sections,digitized axes or independent named-current identity validation. Fixed southward180degree component for Mindanao and west-coast Leeuwin;225degree southwest component for Oyashio;one frame retained through depth. Latitude sections are not independently flow-normal widths.",
    "The frozen North Brazil selector requires complete finite upper0–200m support,surface component>5cm/s,upper200m core above the current primary threshold and positive signed trapezoidal integral. Mindanao/Oyashio primary10cm/s,Leeuwin5cm/s. First native increasing-longitude index breaks maximum-integral ties. No gate enlargement,within-run section replacement,weaker interior substitution or threshold substitution occurs after outcomes.",
    "Oyashio additionally requires native100m model in-situ temperature<=5degC before choosing the integral maximum. JMA official HTML describes this temperature index for141–148E;OSW explicitly extends it upstream/outside that longitude range. Returned HYCOM sea_water_temperature unitsdegC,commentin-situ,exact times and nativeUV/TSgrids were independently checked in cloud. Retain all temperature scalars and gate decisions,including missing/warm rejections. This is neither a JMA observed analysis nor a velocity-axis/bottom definition;cold eddies and unrelated cold currents may pass.",
    "Thermally disqualified neighbors do not become velocity-support gaps. Complete finite upper200m velocity support controls support-edge flags. A maximum at a gate edge or beside missing upper200m support remains unresolved;it is never replaced by a weaker interior candidate. A no-qualifying case remains represented with no selected column or invented depth. Interior status is only a numerical reference bracket,not independent current-axis validation.",
    "All5/10/20cm/s connected-layer diagnoses use the same selected horizontal column,each with its own upper200m qualifying core,adjacent finite crossing brackets,upper/lower statuses and censoring bounds. A nonzero upper crossing stays explicit;native0m is a boundary only for contiguous threshold support. No missing level,deep domain bound or sampled seabed is converted into a physical current bottom. Model paired span and physical thickness remain distinct.",
    "Mindanao identity is the surface southward regional branch14.3N–5.5N,excluding the northward undercurrent,downstreamITF/NECC/EUC and named eddy circuits. Retained near-surface1982–1998bifurcation convention informs context only,not actual2022endpoints;publisher reopen failed this turn and no new original figure review is claimed.",
    "Oyashio46.2N–40N sections may contain coastal/offshore intrusion branches and mixed eddies. JMA source HTML was freshly reviewed;no newQiu2019figure digitization occurred. Fixed southwest component and cold-water screen cannot by themselves establish current-versus-eddy identity,branch continuity or a measured southern limit.",
    "Leeuwin coverage is west-coast22–34S only,explicitly partial relative to the published NorthWestCape–GreatAustralianBight naming convention. The eastward southern continuation,SouthAustralian/Zeehan currents,NWShelf and equatorward undercurrent are excluded. The180degree geographic frame does not reproduce the earlier348degree mooring frame or permit an unqualified comparison with its seasonal mean zerocrossings.",
    "Source coordinate axes were read first;bounded contiguous3–150column slices,exact00Ztime,instantaneous declaration,40positive-down metre levels,componentdimensions/standardnames/units/plausibility and latitude tolerance checked. All cell-pair and decodedbyte budgets were checked before field access. Source-wire hashes and wire-byte totals are not instrumented;retained decoded hashes concern the saved decoded values only.",
    "Twenty-three cloud tests cover12frozen connected-layer cases and11new cases:thermal gating beforeselection,inclusive5degC boundary,missing/warm/no-fallback outcomes,thermal-vs-velocity support edges,invalid scaling,nonthermal frozen-selector equivalence,different primary thresholds,ties/local peaks,signed geographic counterflow,full native cycliclongitude gates,vertical gaps and retained owner/time/frame/component/temperature-hash mutation audits. Each actual retained section is recomputed and audited in cloud.",
    "Collection and tests ran sequentially in cloud on one idle CPU. Local work prepared code/metadata,reviewed primary text and metadata,checked exact hashes and retained source artifacts;no local numerical field processing/tests or runtime/UI/native/WASM/browser/server work. Publication uses unchanged fixed byte caps with separate small batches.",
    "These are two instantaneous assimilating-model snapshots,not independent direct observations,monthly means,annual extrema or seasonal envelopes. No physical whole-route depth profile,matched width/volume join,state passage or global total is admitted. Canonical depth registerv48and regional projection inventoryv1remain unchanged by source retention;new regional projections require their own pinned additive inventory. Eddy size baseline stays unchanged."
  ],
